    "narrative": "Today\u2019s optimal lineup for Ghost Ride the WHIP centers on three high-ceiling plays that provide both stability and the coveted stolen base upside we prioritize. **Vinnie Pasquantino** leads the charge with a 76.21 efficiency score, benefiting from an excellent matchup against Arrighetti, whose 4.73 xERA signals significant opportunities for run production in the heart of our order. Meanwhile, **Corbin Carroll** (73.35) and **Mickey Moniak** (73.14) are locked in as our primary engines for speed; **Mickey Moniak** specifically sees a massive +14% boost due to his dynamic platoon advantage, while **Corbin Carroll** continues to capitalize on favorable park factors. **Trevor Story** also warrants mention, as his 70.35 score is heavily bolstered by a +16% park adjustment, making him a critical weapon against Bradish today.\n\nThe most difficult decision on the bench involved **Josh Naylor**, who missed the starting cut with a 55.62 score. While he remains a strong asset, he was edged out by the superior platoon and positional efficiency provided by **Isaac Paredes** and **Gabriel Moreno**. The optimizer prioritized the specific matchup advantages of our starters over the marginal gains **Josh Naylor** offered against Jump. Looking at the broader roster, **James Wood** is a must-start at 67.15; his elite 0.417 xwOBA and the added aggressive baserunning potential against Wrobleski\u2019s slow delivery make him the most efficient leadoff choice we have. Note that **Seiya Suzuki** is confirmed for an active start, though we are monitoring the lineup for **Griffin Conine**, whose 49.97 score is the lowest in the current lineup; if any late-breaking weather or lineup changes occur, he would be the first candidate to be replaced by a more stable bench piece.",
